<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net"><diagram id="p_02_one_event_path" name="02-one-event-path"><mxGraphModel dx="800" dy="600" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1280" pageHeight="673" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="title" value="One event, one path: the kernel orders, admits and intercepts every input first; the reducer sees only what is left, and nothing is sent until one snapshot is committed" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=17;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="12" width="1240" height="48" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s0" value="perception" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="84" width="150" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s1" value="reasoner turn results" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="116" width="150" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s2" value="motion-layer outcomes" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="148" width="150" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s3" value="timers" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="180" width="150" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s4" value="operator" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="212" width="150" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s5" value="simulation" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="244" width="150" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="srch" value="INPUTS -&gt; typed events" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="64" width="150" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="queue" value="1  ONE BOUNDED PRIORITY QUEUE, ONE WORKER&#10;&#10;priority order:&#10;1 safety  &gt;  2 reset  &gt;  3 operator control  &gt;  4 correlated command outcomes  &gt;  5 observations&#10;&#10;inside one priority, a total order from: normalised observation time -&gt; source rank -&gt; source sequence -&gt; event ID (Lamport 1978: a deterministic tie-break yields one order every replay agrees on)&#10;&#10;replay uses the recorded accepted order" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="215" y="74" width="300" height="200" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="admit" value="2  ADMISSION  (checks the event context: source, sequence, times, clock domain, epoch, uncertainty, session, generation, command)&#10;&#10;REJECTED, never reaching the reducer:&#10;- stale, duplicate, wrong generation, wrong session, wrong command&#10;- an outcome for a command that is not pending&#10;- age or timestamp uncertainty over its bound&#10;- a participant-bound input whose track is not the current participant track&#10;- a source not admitted for this target (B5: rejected before queue insertion)&#10;&#10;rejected, NOT deferred: queueing would let one visitor's content reach the next" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="545" y="74" width="340" height="200" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="icpt" value="3  INTERCEPTION  (the kernel handles these itself)&#10;&#10;safety and reset | readiness assessment, refresh, loss | start and yield of the idle 'ready' behaviour | visitor-audio permit issue, revoke, refusal | runtime faults and queue overflow | operator abort | participant retirement needing cleanup | cleanup acknowledgements and the cleanup deadline | the startup proof that every store is clean&#10;&#10;No experience may override, delay or reject any of them. The kernel then derives the TENTATIVE envelope." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="915" y="74" width="335" height="200" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="red" value="4  REDUCER (the experience)&#10;pure: (local state, read-only envelope, event) -&gt; (next local state, ordered effects)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="320" width="190" height="84" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="val" value="5  VALIDATE, in order:&#10;kernel invariants (cannot be waived) -&gt; story invariants -&gt; every effect" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="236" y="320" width="190" height="84" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ids" value="6  DERIVE COMMAND IDs&#10;deterministically, so a re-dispatch is idempotent" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="442" y="320" width="190" height="84" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="mat" value="7  MATERIALISE commands and verify the tentative snapshot" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="648" y="320" width="190" height="84" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="cmt" value="8  COMMIT ONE SNAPSHOT&#10;envelope + local state + pending commands + leases + timers" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=3;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="854" y="320" width="190" height="84" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dsp" value="9  DISPATCH&#10;in effect order, through the catalog to the per-target adapters" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1060" y="320" width="190" height="84" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="fail_pre" value="Any failure in steps 4-7: NOTHING is committed and NOTHING is dispatched. A rejected event in step 2 never reaches the reducer, so no experience can act on it by mistake." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="418" width="808" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="outbox" value="Transactional outbox: state and intent are recorded together, then sent; a fast completion can never arrive before the state that records its command." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="854" y="418" width="190" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="fail_post" value="A dispatcher failure AFTER commit takes the correlated failure path; it never erases or invents command state." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1060" y="418" width="190" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="safety" value="Safety sorts first and is still typed and admitted. Preemption is proven from every local state of every registered experience (C2). Software preemption is additive: the guaranteed stop is a hardware relay in the emergency-stop loop (B4)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="470" width="808" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="legend" value="Legend:  amber = kernel-owned steps  |  green = the one step the experience owns  |  blue = inputs and dispatch targets  |  red = what failure means  |  thick border = the commit point. One worker processes one event at a time: a public stand produces few events per second, so replayability, not throughput, is the constraint." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="528" width="1220" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="sources" value="Sources. Mechanisms: this kit's notes/ (named per line below) and glossary.md. Every number is loaded from ../constants.json by the key shown: [Pn] = public (cited); [In] = illustrative (a round design parameter that keeps the design's relations; never a measurement of any system); [calc] = my arithmetic on tagged values.&#10;Mechanism: notes/B4-kernel-interception-and-arbitration.md (intercepted classes, one ordered queue, priority and tie-break, admission rejections, rejection not deferral, single worker, hardware stop); B3-the-effect-vocabulary.md (atomic preparation and dispatch steps, transactional outbox, deterministic command IDs); B5 (target-scoped producer admission); C2 (preemption from every local state). Public: Lamport, 'Time, clocks, and the ordering of events in a distributed system', Communications 21(7), 1978; Richardson, 'Pattern: Transactional outbox', microservices.io. Step numbers on this page are a drawing order, not the numbering in the notes. This page carries no numeric design parameter." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="582" width="1220" height="75" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge0" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.115;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s0" target="queue"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge1" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.275;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s1" target="queue"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge2" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.435;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s2" target="queue"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge3" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.595;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s3" target="queue"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge4" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.755;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s4" target="queue"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge5" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.915;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s5" target="queue"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge6" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontColor=#d79b00;" edge="1" parent="1" source="queue" target="admit"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge7" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontColor=#d79b00;" edge="1" parent="1" source="admit" target="icpt"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge8" value="delegate only what is left" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontColor=#d79b00;" edge="1" parent="1" source="icpt" target="red"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1082" y="297" /><mxPoint x="125" y="297" /></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge9" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="red" target="val"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge10" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="val" target="ids"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge11" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="ids" target="mat"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge12" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="mat" target="cmt"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge13" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="cmt" target="dsp"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>